# Authoritative line-ending policy for the repo.
# This file is the single source of truth and overrides each developer's local
# core.autocrlf / core.eol settings, so endings are deterministic on every
# machine and in CI. All text files are stored as LF in git AND checked out as
# LF in the working tree on every OS (eol=lf), so `dotnet format` agrees
# everywhere — Windows, macOS, and the Linux CI runner. Visual Studio, Rider
# and VS Code all handle LF files on Windows without issue.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Verify snapshot files: must stay LF on every OS or snapshot comparisons break
# across platforms. (received files are git-ignored but normalized defensively.)
*.verified.txt text eol=lf
*.received.txt text eol=lf

# Binary assets git must never normalize.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.snk  binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.pdf  binary
